# No Git History Unless Asked

## Default

**Do not** look into, search, or summarize git history unless the user **explicitly** asks for it.

## Do not (unless asked)

- `git log`, `git blame`, `git show`, `git reflog`
- Browsing old commits, diffs against past SHAs, or commit message archaeology
- Inferring intent, authorship, or “how this used to work” from history

## Allowed without a history ask

- Current working tree only when needed for the task: `git status`, `git diff` (unstaged/staged)
- Git operations the user explicitly requested (commit, PR, branch, etc.), using only the history those steps require

## When history is allowed

Only after a clear request, e.g. “look at git history”, “who changed this”, “what changed in commit X”, or “compare to last release”.
